[[:db/retract 17592186198714 :question/answer-fields 17592186194910] {:db/id 17592186198714 :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n- $P(x):$ $2x+1\\le 7$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x>1$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & \\le 7 \\\\ 2x & \\le 6 \\\\ x & \\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,3]$\nand its complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(3,\\infty ).$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n${T}_{Q}=(1,\\infty )$ \nand its complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}=(-\\infty ,1].$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & =(-\\infty ,3]\\cap (1,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(1,3] \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & =(3,\\infty )\\cap (-\\infty ,1] \\\\  & =∅ \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & =(1,3]\\cup ∅ \\\\  & =(1,3].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-19a2472e-e7b5-5d8b-b209-032b85345908"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-19a2472e-e7b5-5d8b-b209-032b85345908" :answer-field/id #uuid "19a2472e-e7b5-5d8b-b209-032b85345908" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b147d43c-2609-5b72-9008-d1eaeff9e457" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b147d43c-2609-5b72-9008-d1eaeff9e457" "answer-b6a2f396-444c-5e43-bd1f-a8b609b95e23" "answer-fac2b16b-87a5-55df-b80e-8c4009dba8e6" "answer-87bbd064-d59f-57df-8f61-e9b023cda8fb" "answer-906bdee1-f182-5897-9585-c900d8130cd0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b147d43c-2609-5b72-9008-d1eaeff9e457" :answer/id #uuid "b147d43c-2609-5b72-9008-d1eaeff9e457" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6a2f396-444c-5e43-bd1f-a8b609b95e23" :answer/id #uuid "b6a2f396-444c-5e43-bd1f-a8b609b95e23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fac2b16b-87a5-55df-b80e-8c4009dba8e6" :answer/id #uuid "fac2b16b-87a5-55df-b80e-8c4009dba8e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87bbd064-d59f-57df-8f61-e9b023cda8fb" :answer/id #uuid "87bbd064-d59f-57df-8f61-e9b023cda8fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-3,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-906bdee1-f182-5897-9585-c900d8130cd0" :answer/id #uuid "906bdee1-f182-5897-9585-c900d8130cd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198259 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f02a6ca7-3a4a-592a-bdf2-d7236cdc3430"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f02a6ca7-3a4a-592a-bdf2-d7236cdc3430" :question/id #uuid "f02a6ca7-3a4a-592a-bdf2-d7236cdc3430" :question/math-academy-id "q-183319" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇒Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$ \n\n- $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}\\le 9$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $5x-3>7$" :question/worked-solution "Since $P(x)⇒Q(x)≡¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={T}_{¬P∨Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{¬P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\le 9 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is \n${T}_{P}=[-3,3].$ \nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$\n\n- To find the the truth set of $Q(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-3 & >7 \\\\ 5x & >10 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $Q(x)$ is\n${T}_{Q}=(2,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =((-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ))\\cup (2,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c0c1a066-5f9e-50ca-b88c-ecae2c88919a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c0c1a066-5f9e-50ca-b88c-ecae2c88919a" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0c1a066-5f9e-50ca-b88c-ecae2c88919a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-387aad0d-bb8f-5b82-9e3e-546a38a316a5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-387aad0d-bb8f-5b82-9e3e-546a38a316a5" "answer-593a82e8-9e86-54b3-98d9-66e1b119d3aa" "answer-f6a5945c-de3e-54a9-85e3-ea79b0853ec9" "answer-acc753ba-6cdc-5e6f-a65f-cf4670d35ffc" "answer-9ef73a8c-ede8-54cc-8ecc-ab3bcf027fd6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-387aad0d-bb8f-5b82-9e3e-546a38a316a5" :answer/id #uuid "387aad0d-bb8f-5b82-9e3e-546a38a316a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-593a82e8-9e86-54b3-98d9-66e1b119d3aa" :answer/id #uuid "593a82e8-9e86-54b3-98d9-66e1b119d3aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6a5945c-de3e-54a9-85e3-ea79b0853ec9" :answer/id #uuid "f6a5945c-de3e-54a9-85e3-ea79b0853ec9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acc753ba-6cdc-5e6f-a65f-cf4670d35ffc" :answer/id #uuid "acc753ba-6cdc-5e6f-a65f-cf4670d35ffc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-3,2]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ef73a8c-ede8-54cc-8ecc-ab3bcf027fd6" :answer/id #uuid "9ef73a8c-ede8-54cc-8ecc-ab3bcf027fd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-54b12d24-977a-54a5-aff6-9e8057c5e326" "question-4d6a13d3-ad69-5578-b6a3-a3b3842749f5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-54b12d24-977a-54a5-aff6-9e8057c5e326" :question/id #uuid "54b12d24-977a-54a5-aff6-9e8057c5e326" :question/math-academy-id "q-183351" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $x$ is a multiple of $10,$ then $x$ is a multiple of $5.$\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $10.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $5.$\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x$ is not is a multiple of $10.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not a multiple of $10,$ or $x$ is a multiple of $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9bd67cf2-d2ad-524e-abec-5dd4e6b10fcb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9bd67cf2-d2ad-524e-abec-5dd4e6b10fcb" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bd67cf2-d2ad-524e-abec-5dd4e6b10fcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f76ee12c-807a-54bc-af4b-5d50d1a1d4ed" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a18ce88-661b-56f1-ab50-d4c0c0d859f1" "answer-2d2d1990-533d-5e81-9481-787518e95fc1" "answer-3b95cf79-290b-5ce6-acbf-d836c52800ad" "answer-f76ee12c-807a-54bc-af4b-5d50d1a1d4ed" "answer-0f7f518c-488c-5d96-b7a5-43db3205b127"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a18ce88-661b-56f1-ab50-d4c0c0d859f1" :answer/id #uuid "2a18ce88-661b-56f1-ab50-d4c0c0d859f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x$ is a multiple of $10,$ and $x$ is a multiple of $5.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d2d1990-533d-5e81-9481-787518e95fc1" :answer/id #uuid "2d2d1990-533d-5e81-9481-787518e95fc1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x$ is a multiple of $10,$ or $x$ is a multiple of $5.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b95cf79-290b-5ce6-acbf-d836c52800ad" :answer/id #uuid "3b95cf79-290b-5ce6-acbf-d836c52800ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x$ is not a multiple of $10,$ and $x$ is a multiple of $5.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f76ee12c-807a-54bc-af4b-5d50d1a1d4ed" :answer/id #uuid "f76ee12c-807a-54bc-af4b-5d50d1a1d4ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x$ is not a multiple of $10,$ or $x$ is a multiple of $5.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f7f518c-488c-5d96-b7a5-43db3205b127" :answer/id #uuid "0f7f518c-488c-5d96-b7a5-43db3205b127" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x$ is not a multiple of $10,$ or $x$ is not a multiple of $5.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4d6a13d3-ad69-5578-b6a3-a3b3842749f5" :question/id #uuid "4d6a13d3-ad69-5578-b6a3-a3b3842749f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-183354" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\ge 2.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $-x\\le -2.$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\n- If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ and if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n- $x\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $-x\\le -2.$\n- If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ or if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$" :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\ge 2$ if and only if $-x\\le -2.$\n\n- $x\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $-x\\le -2.$\n\n- If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ and if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-27e45ba6-a42f-5129-95cb-6948d10b75e5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-27e45ba6-a42f-5129-95cb-6948d10b75e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "27e45ba6-a42f-5129-95cb-6948d10b75e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1f5642c9-3238-501d-b001-abe804dbf74b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1f5642c9-3238-501d-b001-abe804dbf74b" "answer-c9063210-0eaf-5f51-9f26-d06d56f1944e" "answer-49d6bd5f-dc44-5b25-a899-60660d018a65" "answer-ead9dfa3-e4dc-59d6-a1e9-1696a9df2aa0" "answer-42236876-92a9-57f6-83c9-30fca5f7268d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f5642c9-3238-501d-b001-abe804dbf74b" :answer/id #uuid "1f5642c9-3238-501d-b001-abe804dbf74b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9063210-0eaf-5f51-9f26-d06d56f1944e" :answer/id #uuid "c9063210-0eaf-5f51-9f26-d06d56f1944e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49d6bd5f-dc44-5b25-a899-60660d018a65" :answer/id #uuid "49d6bd5f-dc44-5b25-a899-60660d018a65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ead9dfa3-e4dc-59d6-a1e9-1696a9df2aa0" :answer/id #uuid "ead9dfa3-e4dc-59d6-a1e9-1696a9df2aa0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42236876-92a9-57f6-83c9-30fca5f7268d" :answer/id #uuid "42236876-92a9-57f6-83c9-30fca5f7268d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-c363db75-51e2-54dd-b22d-923d77f8fec9" :activity/id #uuid "c363db75-51e2